> ### TLDR;
> 
> **Can I automate my emails with Claude?** Yes. By using the Claude Desktop app's Gmail connector and Claude Cowork, you can train Claude on your past sent emails to learn your writing style. You can then create a scheduled daily task where Claude reads your unread emails and automatically generates draft responses in your unique voice.

## The End of Manual Emailing

We've all been there: staring at an inbox full of routine questions, knowing exactly what to say, but lacking the energy to type it all out again.

A friend recently asked me, *"Can I just automate my emails with Claude?"*

Most people assume building an AI email assistant requires complex Zapier integrations, API keys, or coding knowledge. But the landscape has shifted. You can now build a fully automated, highly personalized email workflow in under 60 seconds using off-the-shelf features inside Claude.

Here is the exact, zero-code framework to put your inbox on autopilot.

### Step 1: Connect Gmail to the Claude Desktop App

To get started, you need to give Claude secure access to your inbox context.

1. Download and open the [**Claude Desktop app**](https://claude.com/download).
1. Navigate to your connector settings.
1. Select **Gmail** as your primary data connector.

This bridge allows Claude to securely read the context of your threads without you having to copy and paste walls of text.

### Step 2: Train Claude on Your Unique Tone of Voice

An AI email assistant is only useful if it actually sounds like you. Nobody wants to send emails that sound like a robot wrote them.

Once your Gmail is connected, open a new chat and use this exact prompt structure:

> *"Please read through every email I have responded to in the last 30 days. Learn how I write and respond to emails and turn that into a skill."*

Save this output as a **Skill** within your Claude workspace. You now have a digital clone of your communication style ready to be deployed.

### Step 3: Automate Daily Drafts with Claude Cowork

This is where the real magic happens. Instead of manually prompting Claude every time you get an email, we are going to use **Claude Cowork** to schedule the work for you.

1. Open **Claude Cowork**.
1. Create a **New Scheduled Task**.
1. Set the trigger for your preferred time (e.g., Every weekday at 8:00 AM).
1. Assign the task:

```
"Check my unread emails for the day and draft responses for each based on the email writing skill we have. Ignore promotional emails. Ask clarifying questions if needed before drafting. Brief me about important alerts where I must take an action but need no response."
```

### The Final Review

Your automation is now live. Every morning, while you are pouring your coffee, Claude is reading, analyzing, and drafting your replies.

All that is left for you to do is open your drafts folder, briefly review the AI-generated responses for accuracy, and hit send. You maintain complete control over what goes out, but you eliminate 90% of the friction required to get there.
